  "_meta": {
    "source": "data/Deck Lists/GB2 Opponent Deck Guide (Alamedyang, English-patch names).txt -- Pokemon Card GB2: Here Comes The Great Team Rocket! (Japan-only GBC sequel), decks extracted by the guide's author from actual save data with a hex editor",
    "retrieved": "2026-08-14",
    "scope": "Eight named, flavor-titled opponent decks from GB2 Island (the guide's sections T1-T8) -- the personality-forward picks out of ~45 GB2-Island opponents, chosen over the plain numbered ones per Trevor's ask. Reference data -- NOTHING READS THIS YET.",
    "resolution": "Every entry resolved against data/raw/base1-3.json and base5.json by name, preferring base1 > base2 > base3 > base5 when a name exists in more than one (a handful of cards -- Mr. Mime, Scyther, Kangaskhan, and a few Team Rocket Dark-Pokemon reprints -- exist at two printed numbers within the same set; the lower number was picked arbitrarily, it doesn't matter which for play). All eight total exactly 60 with subs included.",
    "playable_today": "Only allison_psychic_battle needs nothing beyond base1/base2/base3, which are already live -- it's playable as-is right now, confirmed against the live Engine.prototype.validateDeck: ok:true, no errors, no warnings, 14 Basics. Every other deck in this file has at least one `subs` entry and needs base5 (Team Rocket) live at minimum.",
    "subs_kinds": {
      "future-set": "A real printed card that exists in the corpus, just not in a live set yet. Currently only Bill's Teleporter, which is a Neo Genesis (neo1) card -- every one of these eight decks that uses it needs Neo Genesis live, not just Team Rocket, which is a much later milestone than base5 alone would suggest.",
      "unresolved-exclusive": "The GB2 guide's Vending/S-Deck/B-Deck/Gameboy-Dark prefixes -- promotional or video-game-only prints with no real TCG equivalent found anywhere in the corpus (checked against all 14 sets, not just the 3 live ones). These need an actual substitution decision (which real card stands in) before the deck is playable, the same kind of call gbc_decks.json's `subs` table already makes for the GBC1 roster -- not made here, since it wants a real decision rather than an automated one."
    },
    "correction": "The original research pass (DECK_RESEARCH_NOTES.md / OPPONENT_DECK_POOL.md) claimed Allison's Ultra Removal deck was playable today with zero substitution, on the grounds that it has no Rocket-prefixed cards. That was wrong -- it runs 4x Bill's Teleporter, a real card, but from Neo Genesis. Caught only once this file's automated name-resolution pass ran the card past the actual corpus instead of just scanning for known GBC-exclusive prefixes. OPPONENT_DECK_POOL.md's table has been corrected to match."
  },
